aluation: Discarding T8 preserves key sequences and sets up potential for multiple Chows, while removing a terminal tile that's less critical for forming high-point patterns.\nReason: Keeping W4-W5-W6 (Character), B4-B5-B6 (Dot), and T4-T5 (Bamboo) allows for three Chows if a T6 is drawn. Discarding T8 (a terminal) avoids losing any sequence potential and maintains the chance for All Chows (2 points) and Fully Concealed (4 points), totaling 6 points. This is a safer option compared to risking a sequence by discarding B5 or B6.\nAnswer: Play T8"}
